---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Noticias from '../../components/Noticias.astro';
import Logos from '../../components/Logos.astro';
import Social from '../../components/Social.astro';
import { fichaUAH } from '../../i18n';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base titulo="Home" lang="en">
  <header class="post-header">
    <h1 class="post-title"><span class="negrita">MESH</span></h1>
    <p class="post-description">Multilayer Enhanced Structural metaHeuristics for distributed optimization.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="clearfix">
    <div class="profile">
      <div class="address">
        <p>University of Alcalá</p>
        <p>MICIU / AEI</p>
        <p>Knowledge Generation Projects 2025</p>
        <p>Sep 2026 – Aug 2029</p>
        <p>Ref. PID2025-174033NA-I00</p>
        <p>PI: Enrique de la Hoz</p>
        <p>PI: Luis de la Cruz</p>
        <p><a href={fichaUAH} rel="noopener">UAH research portal entry</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p>
      MESH is a research project at the <a href="https://www.uah.es/en/">University of Alcalá</a> on the
      <strong>optimisation of distributed systems</strong>: communication networks, urban traffic, the Internet of
      Things or cyber-resilience mechanisms. Optimising them is hard for three reasons that compound each other:
      their scale, the hidden interrelationships among their elements and the feedback loops those relationships
      produce.
    </p>
    <p>
      Classical metaheuristics scale well but are blind to the structure of the problem. Message-passing and
      negotiation techniques exploit that structure, but scale poorly. Graph neural networks have shown that using
      the structure inside the algorithm itself changes performance. MESH brings that idea to optimisation: it models
      each system as a <a href={`${base}/en/proyecto`}>multilayer factor graph</a> and designs algorithms that
      natively exploit the relationships the graph expresses.
    </p>
    <p>
      On this site we publish the project's <a href={`${base}/en/resultados`}>results</a> as they consolidate, its
      <a href={`${base}/en/publicaciones`}>publications</a> and the <a href={`${base}/en/recursos`}>datasets,
      software and models</a> we release so that experiments can be reproduced.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>news</h2>
  <Noticias lang="en" />
  <Logos lang="en" />
  <Social />
</Base>
